# Article: Pack (adversaries)

Roles: coder, reviewer.

Chain: coder -> reviewer -> coder.

- coder implements a slice, then sends a git_handoff to reviewer.
- reviewer adversarially reviews the merged result. Findings that require
  changes go back to coder as a git_handoff carrying the review commit;
  that first handoff authorizes one repair (coder fixes and re-forwards to
  reviewer). A clean review's return handoff is TERMINAL: coder merges it
  and stops. If the repair still earns a finding, reviewer stops and reports
  the blocker to the user; it does not start a second repair loop.
